# Merge policy for the changelog.
#
# Every branch adds its entry at the top of a section in `CHANGELOG.md`, so two
# concurrent branches insert different text at the same anchor. Git has no basis
# on which to order them and stops with a conflict -- even though both sides are
# pure additions and the resolution is always "keep both".
#
# `union` tells git to do exactly that: concatenate both sides rather than stop.
#
# Two things to know before relying on it:
#
#   * It is safe only while this file stays APPEND-ONLY. An entry EDITED on two
#     branches is silently duplicated instead of raising a conflict. Correct an
#     existing entry on one branch only, and read the result afterwards.
#   * It applies to merges and rebases run by git -- which is to say, locally.
#     GitHub's merge button does not read this file, so a pull request still
#     reports a changelog conflict in the web UI; what changes is that rebasing
#     the branch onto main resolves it without anyone editing anything.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
